    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "where the notation $\\sim(a,b)$ means that the random variable has mean $a$ and variance $b$. On the other hand, the mixed model partitions the vector of residual effects into two components, with $e^{*}=Z\\mathbf{u}+\\mathbf{e}$, giving",
